# Environment Architecture

The [airhockey](mdc:airhockey) package provides environment/task wrappers around lower-level simulators.

## High-Level Layers

- Base environment interface and shared behavior: [airhockey/airhockey_base.py](mdc:airhockey/airhockey_base.py)
- Task-level wrappers and variants:
  - [airhockey/airhockey_tasks](mdc:airhockey/airhockey_tasks)
  - [airhockey/airhockey_simple_tasks.py](mdc:airhockey/airhockey_simple_tasks.py)
  - [airhockey/airhockey_hierarchical_tasks.py](mdc:airhockey/airhockey_hierarchical_tasks.py)
- Reward-specific logic: [airhockey/airhockey_rewards](mdc:airhockey/airhockey_rewards)

## Simulator Backends

- Simulator adapters live in [airhockey/sims](mdc:airhockey/sims)
- Real-world adapter: [airhockey/sims/air_hockey_real.py](mdc:airhockey/sims/air_hockey_real.py)
- Box2D adapter: [airhockey/sims/airhockey_box2d.py](mdc:airhockey/sims/airhockey_box2d.py)
- Shared simulator abstractions/utilities: [airhockey/sims/airhockey_sim.py](mdc:airhockey/sims/airhockey_sim.py)

## Guidance For Edits

- Keep env/task wrappers separated from low-level simulator-specific behavior.
- Place simulator-specific changes under `airhockey/sims` and keep task APIs stable where possible.
